IPlayerContext.player() returns Player (not LocalPlayer), minecraft() the game-thread event loop (Minecraft or MinecraftServer),
entities() is implemented by the host instead of casting to ClientLevel, and mouseSensitivity() is a new defaulted method
(replaces a read of the client options). IPlayerController and RotationUtils take Player.
IBaritoneProvider: getBaritoneForPlayer(Player); createBaritone takes a factory for the player context;
getBaritoneForMinecraft/getBaritoneForConnection (client only) are dropped.

